# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs entrypoint.sh, which starts Elasticsearch and then
# Kibana 6.5.4 with the vulnerable Timelion plugin ENABLED, in the background,
# and finally execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * Kibana is ALREADY RUNNING with Timelion enabled when the agent starts,
#     which makes the "set timelion.enabled:false but never restarted Kibana"
#     case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Kibana cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART Kibana after disabling Timelion,
# not merely edit kibana.yml.
